# RuForge — filled-in color contract (worked example)

A concrete, filled-in version of the per-project contract from `design-style` §4. Use this as the pattern for how to fill in a new project. NOT as a global default to copy blindly.

RuForge is a media app, so it's **dark** (long watches in dark rooms), and each section carries its own **tonal hue**.

## RuForge Home — warm/cozy (espresso + sand-gold)
```
THEME MODE:  dark
BASE HUE:    warm espresso brown
ACCENT:      sand-gold
COLOR MODE:  MONOCHROME (accent carries action/active)

--surface-0: #1c1512;   /* espresso base */
--surface-1: #261d18;
--surface-2: #322620;
--surface-3: #3e2f27;
--accent:    #EDCF9B;   /* sand-gold */
--text-strong:  #f5ede4;
--text-default: #d8cabb;
--text-muted:   #9a8a7a;
```

## RuForge Music — red (YouTube Music kinship)
```
THEME MODE:  dark
BASE HUE:    near-black with a faint red lean
ACCENT:      red
COLOR MODE:  MONOCHROME

--surface-0: #0e0a0a;
--surface-1: #181111;
--surface-2: #221717;
--accent:    #e53935;   /* tune to match the music-app red */
```
Album art: 1:1 square, `object-fit: cover`, rounded. NEVER letterboxed on black (this is the named anti-pattern from this exact screen).

## RuForge Movies — purple / cinematic (planned)
```
THEME MODE:  dark
BASE HUE:    deep cinematic charcoal-violet
ACCENT:      purple
COLOR MODE:  MONOCHROME
```
Lean into the Cineby cinematic-hero model: full-bleed hero art, long bottom scrim, solid transparent nav, poster (2:3) cards for browse rows, 16:9 thumbnails for continue-watching.

## Notes
- Hue lives in the surface ramp, not just the accent. "Dark" here means warm-dark or red-dark, not pure `#000`.
- One accent per section. Music's red ≠ Home's gold; they're different surfaces of the same app, each themed to its job.
- Values above are starting points; tune against the real references for each section.
